    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.** serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) is the clear start of the day; the combination of a favorable matchup against Montero and a distinct boost from favorable winds allows his dynamic platoon profile to shine. **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.92) also offers high-end upside against the left-handed P\u00e9rez; while there is a 31% rain risk, his profile against southpaws remains a focal point of our efficiency model. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) rounds out our top tier, as his aggressive matchup against the veteran Scherzer provides the necessary leverage to maximize production in our 5x5 context.\n\nWe are paying close attention to the bottom of our order, specifically the inclusion of **Nasim Nunez** (62.09). Despite hitting ninth, **Nasim Nunez** earns his spot through significant SP skill advantages and our internal weighting for speed, which we prioritize to keep pace in the scarce SB category. **Jacob Wilson** (64.30) similarly benefits from an excellent park factor that boosts his efficiency despite the SP matchup. **Curtis Mead** (55.09) sits as our lowest-rated starter, narrowly avoiding the bench because his 10% park boost offsets a difficult pairing with Perkins. **Coby Mayo** (51.73) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; his base projection was strong, but he ultimately ceded the utility spot to **Jacob Wilson** due to the latter\u2019s superior order position and park-adjusted environment. \n\nCaution is advised regarding **Drake Baldwin** (61.71) and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as both face the same 31% rain risk that could lead to a shortened game or an outright postponement. We are monitoring the weather closely to ensure we don't burn an unnecessary game cap on a rain-out. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (59.55) sits on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier; while his score is respectable, his matchup against Sproat is neutralized by a negative park factor, forcing us to temper expectations despite his consistent recent performance.",
